{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And it shall be when He brings you, etc.</b> It says <b>and it shall be when He brings you</b>, etc., to say that one must not forget the commandments of HaShem when HaShem expands his borders and he grows fat and kicks. And He did not bother to say 'when,' specifically in the Land, because this is a commandment dependent on the body, and we say in Qiddushin (36b) that any commandment that is dependent on the body makes no distinction between in the Land and outside the Land."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:25.847727989Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}